This file is a developers TODO list.  It is not complete.


- We need to find a replacement for the bash build files:
   lib/glob_cfiles.bash and share/bash-completion/completions/mk_quickplot.bash

   Finding a way to replace lib/glob_cfiles.bash may be difficult given
   meson does not like file name wild cards.

   share/bash-completion/completions/mk_quickplot.bash runs sed.

- PLOT CULLING: The quickplot (libpanels.so) C plotting interface and/or
  code needs to change to accommodate zoom and culling.  We can zoom in a
  lot causing the plotted pixels to be due to round off from a large
  double to an int.  You can end up putting plot points at somewhat random
  looking places when you zoom too far.  Culling out plotted points that
  are out of range needs to be addressed.  Additional user interfaces may
  need to be added to pnGraph and/or pnPlot.  Points may need to be moved
  to just outside the edge of the graph window so that plotted lines stay
  consistent.

- We need to install robust versions of libpixman and libcairo, and run
  the "quick" tests with Valgrind and with the programs linked with the
  robust versions of libpixman and libcairo.



